{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Patel, one of the surgical team. You're here today for your scheduled hernia repair, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been having a lot of pain near my old incision, and they said the hernia was starting to block things a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the imaging showed part of your colon was partially stuck in the hernia. We were able to reduce it, but because the defect is large, surgery is the best option to prevent it from happening again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will you be using mesh? I remember last time they did the Puestow, it was a big surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll be doing a primary repair with Prolene mesh overlay. It helps strengthen the area and reduces the chance of the hernia coming back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And how long will I be out after the surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll stay in the hospital for a few days. We’ll start you on IV fluids and pain medication, and gradually get you back on food once your bowels start working again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had gastroparesis before—will that be a problem?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re aware of your history. We’ll start you on clear liquids on post-op day one and advance slowly. We’ll also continue your pancreatic enzymes and monitor how you tolerate things."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my diabetes—should I take my metformin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. We’ll hold metformin while you’re not eating and switch to insulin if needed. We’ll restart it once you’re on a regular diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, makes sense. What about my other meds—like for my mood and nerves?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll resume most of your psychiatric medications as soon as you’re able to take pills. The team will coordinate with psychiatry to make sure nothing is missed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had some PTSD flare-ups lately—work stuff, old memories. I hope I can sleep okay here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2129-12-22 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can help with that. You’re on prazosin and zolpidem at home—we’ll restart those as appropriate. Let the nurses know if you’re having trouble resting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2129-12-22 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from surgery. The procedure went very well—ventral hernia repair with mesh, no complications. You’re in the recovery unit now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2129-12-22 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks… I feel groggy. Is the drain in my side normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2129-12-22 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we placed a JP drain in your right lower quadrant to collect any fluid and prevent buildup. It will stay in until your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2129-12-22 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the catheter?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2129-12-22 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s temporary. We’ll remove it tonight or tomorrow morning once you’re up and moving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2129-12-22 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pain’s okay right now. I see the PCA button—should I use it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2129-12-22 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, use it as needed. It’s hydromorphone, and it’s safe when used properly. We’ll switch to oral meds once you start eating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2129-12-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs look stable. Glucose was 154 this morning—well controlled. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2129-12-23 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I try some water or ice chips today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2129-12-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start you on clear liquids—water, broth, apple juice. If you tolerate that, we’ll advance your diet tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2129-12-23 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my pain meds—will I still get the PCA?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2129-12-23 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep it for now, but once you’re on oral pain meds, we’ll discontinue it. Chronic pain service reviewed your case and recommended continuing gabapentin and adding acetaminophen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2129-12-23 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m on a lot of meds—can you tell me which ones I’ll restart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2129-12-23 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll restart most: lisinopril, simvastatin, omeprazole, amitriptyline, ziprasidone, duloxetine, gabapentin, metformin once you’re eating, and your pancreatic enzymes with meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2129-12-23 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the stool softener? I don’t want to strain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2129-12-23 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll give you docusate twice a day and senna at night to help. Avoid heavy lifting for at least six weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2129-12-23 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling? Any nausea or pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2129-12-23 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pain is about a 3. I had some broth and jello—no nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2129-12-23 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll upgrade you to a soft diet tomorrow—maybe mashed potatoes, applesauce. And we removed the catheter this morning—you voided fine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2129-12-23 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, no problem. The drain is a little annoying, but I’ll manage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2129-12-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re tolerating food well. We’re advancing you to a regular diet. How’s the pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2129-12-24 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "About a 4, but manageable. I’m on oral meds now—hydromorphone as needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2129-12-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and acetaminophen regularly. We discontinued the PCA. You’re walking well—great job with the ambulation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2129-12-24 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When do I get discharged?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2129-12-24 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If all goes well today, we’re planning for tomorrow morning. You need to tolerate a regular diet, be pain-controlled, and have no fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2129-12-24 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be going home with the drain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2129-12-24 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’ll stay in until your follow-up. You’ll need to empty it daily, keep the site clean, and watch for signs of infection—increased redness, fever, or cloudy drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2129-12-24 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2129-12-24 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll take Keflex four times a day for 14 days to prevent infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2129-12-25 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’ve done well—afebrile, eating, walking, pain controlled. We’re discharging you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2129-12-25 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What about my staples?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2129-12-25 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’ll be removed at your follow-up. You can shower—just pat the area dry. No baths or swimming until then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2129-12-25 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And activity?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2129-12-25 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No lifting over 10 pounds, no driving while on pain meds. Continue walking daily. Follow up with surgery and your PCP in one week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2129-12-25 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I think I understand. I’ll take my meds, care for the drain, and call if anything’s wrong."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2129-12-25 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’re doing great. We’ll see you in clinic to remove the staples and drain. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2129-12-22 08:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2129-12-25 14:07:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old male with a history of chronic pancreatitis, type 2 diabetes, gastroparesis, and prior Puestow procedure was admitted for elective repair of a symptomatic incisional hernia that had caused a minor bowel obstruction. He underwent an uncomplicated open ventral incisional hernia repair with Prolene mesh overlay on hospital day one. Postoperatively, he was managed with IV fluids, antibiotics, a JP drain, and pain control via PCA initially, transitioning to oral medications. His diet was advanced from clear liquids on postoperative day one to a regular diet by day three. He voided independently after catheter removal, remained afebrile, and had stable vital signs. He was discharged home on postoperative day three with instructions for incision and drain care, oral Keflex, and follow-up. His chronic conditions, including hypertension, bipolar disorder, PTSD, and diabetes, were managed with continuation of most home medications.",
    "problems": [
      "Incisional hernia without mention of obstruction or gangrene",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Keloid scar",
      "Posttraumatic stress disorder",
      "Bipolar disorder, unspecified",
      "Other convulsions",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Lumbago"
    ]
  }
}
